From 6813439067f72897dc657248977541315b68f090 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bump Go language level to build against system x/sys

The RPM build discards the vendored golang.org/x/sys and points the
vendor directory at the system golang-x-sys-devel package. On AlmaLinux
10 that is x/sys >= 0.26, whose sources use features that need go1.17+.

The build still forced the go1.16 language level from two places:
- go.mod declares "go 1.16".
- vendor/modules.txt carries no per-module "go" annotation, so it falls
  back to go1.16 for that module, ignoring go.mod.

So, bump the go version to 1.21, so xenstore compiles again.

Signed-off-by: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>
---
 go.mod             | 2 +-
 vendor/modules.txt | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index 272fdf6..2648338 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 module github.com/xenserver/xe-guest-utilities
 
-go 1.16
+go 1.21
 
 require golang.org/x/sys v0.0.0-20210414055047-fe65e336abe0
diff --git a/vendor/modules.txt b/vendor/modules.txt
index c77a673..0169adf 100644
--- a/vendor/modules.txt
+++ b/vendor/modules.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
 # golang.org/x/sys v0.0.0-20210414055047-fe65e336abe0
-## explicit
+## explicit; go 1.21
 golang.org/x/sys/internal/unsafeheader
 golang.org/x/sys/unix
